0..72 Comment "// A model whose sorts are manifest where a model of its theory is asked"
73..140 Comment "// : a model type fixing sorts of a theory takes one forgetting map"
141..218 Comment "// from `Model(T) with sort C = x` to `Model(T)`, at every carrier `x`, which"
219..294 Comment "// puts each fixed sort back as the field it is in the theory\'s record. The"
295..369 Comment "// checker applies it where the one model stands at the other, solving `x`"
370..443 Comment "// from the model\'s type, and the run reads the application. The map is a"
444..521 Comment "// family in the carrier, so a manifest model carried along an equivalence of"
522..599 Comment "// carriers is read alike once forgotten. A model fixing some of its theory\'s"
600..677 Comment "// sorts takes the map putting back those alone, every other sort staying the"
678..749 Comment "// field it is. A model type may fix a sort to another model\'s carrier,"
750..820 Comment "// `with sort C = a.C`, the two then sharing it, and so may one fixing"
821..889 Comment "// another of its sorts, reading a sort the other leaves a field. An"
890..963 Comment "// operation is read off a model\'s binder as a sort is, `a.incr` the step"
964..1037 Comment "// `a`\'s record holds at `a`\'s carrier, whether the carrier is a field or"
1038..1108 Comment "// manifest. An ascription `(m : Model(Counter))` states the crossing,"
1109..1153 Comment "// and the explicit twin writes the map out."
1154..1156 Comment "//"
1157..1172 Comment "// - see: #2120"
1173..1188 Comment "// - see: #2132"
1189..1204 Comment "// - see: #2131"
1205..1220 Comment "// - see: #2158"
1221..1278 Comment "// - see: #2246 — `stepOwn`, `stepZero`, `stepManifest`"
1279..1294 Comment "// - see: #2130"
1296..1371 Comment "// The counter, counting up and down modulo three, the negation between the"
1372..1422 Comment "// counts, and `observe`, which reads any counter."
